WEBVTT

00:01:59.574 --> 00:02:01.993
and joined a queer online community,

00:02:02.034 --> 00:02:04.495
I met people who created
spaces that embraced

00:02:04.495 --> 00:02:07.498
and protected everyone's ability
to be their authentic self.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.960
And this was the first time
that I genuinely felt safe.

00:02:11.002 --> 00:02:12.336
Just one example.

00:02:12.378 --> 00:02:15.506
Blackmail is a huge problem
for the queer community in Kenya.

00:02:15.548 --> 00:02:17.758
Blackmailers can make tons of money

00:02:17.758 --> 00:02:20.636
by threatening to out queer
people to authorities.

00:02:20.678 --> 00:02:23.681
So one queer online community
that I joined when I was younger

00:02:23.723 --> 00:02:26.726
was trying to prevent
and expose known blackmailers.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:30.021
I realized that one of the people
listed as a blackmailer